+ * log ends at tick 25 with no further vsync, unlike log46/47 where only the
+ * boot thread stalled. log49 adds gpu_gbif and shows GBIF was not halted at
+ * all (halt=0 ack=0x3), same ending. So the CM3 only wedges the bus once it
+ * has a clock to run on, which leaves power (CX/MX rail never voted), the
+ * GPU SMMU (GMU buffers are SMMU iovas; QTBL and log are 0) and the CM3's
+ * first memory access as the candidates. 0107 adds gpu_rails=1 (cx.lvl and
+ * mx.lvl to 193), gpu_smmu=1 (read the GPU SMMU GR0 state at 0x5040000) and
+ * gpu_norelease=1, which stops after the preset so the clock and rail
+ * changes can be measured with the CM3 still in reset.
